\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Top: Radial profile of gas particle mass (resolution). Scatter plot shows particle distribution at the time of first sink formation; solid line and shaded region correspond to the mean and $\pm 1\sigma $ for radial profiles across all snapshots after first sink formation. Horizontal lines correspond to $1/2 \Delta m$ of previous resolution region, since our particle splitting algorithm is subdividing parent particles in 2 for each new level of split. Bottom: Same as Top, but for radial profile of equivalent cell size $\Delta x = (\Delta m / \rho )^{1/3}$. }}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
